{
  "id": "COMPOUND:14307 - PROTEIN:5864",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which chlorothiazide may interact with U373 MG cells, through targeting Caspase-5. This is supported by multiple pathways where chlorothiazide is linked to Caspase-5, which in turn is targeted by several compounds, including (2R,3S,4R,5R,6S)-2-[2-(3,4-dihydroxy-5-methoxyphenyl)-7-hydroxy-3-[(2R,3S,4R,5R,6S)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxan-2-yl]oxychromenylium-5-yl]oxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxane-3,4,5-triol and (4S,4aR,5S,8aR,9aS)-4a,5,6,7,8,8a,9,9a-Octahydro-4-hydroxy-9a-methoxy-3,4a,5-trimethylnaphtho(2,3-b)furan-2(4H)-one. These compounds are all implicated in the targeting of U373 MG cells, indicating a possible role in cell death pathways. The presence of multiple distinct compounds targeting Caspase-5 suggests that chlorothiazide may exert its effects through a mechanism involving Caspase-5 inhibition, potentially leading to apoptosis in U373 MG cells. The evidence is consistent with a mechanistic link, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
